for various reasons (inherent bugs, improper installation, system crash,
etc.) nethack games can crash during play and in some cases it is not
possible to reconstruct the pieces. a backup of the current save file
provides some measure of security in these cases. nethack game maintainers
should consider a "shell-script" that runs nethack that implements:
[copy saved games to backup directory]
[start the game]
this, unfortunately, makes it possible to cheat but that's a function of
the ethics and morality of the dungeoneers involved.

